            <ArticleTitle>Ectopic atrial rhythm with progressively increasing exit block.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>92-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of ectopic atrial rhythm with progressively increasing exit block is reported in a case of ischemic heart disease. Such a rhythm suggests significantly diseased atria which are unable to sustain a regular rhythm for a long period. This arrhythmia should warn the clinician of impending atrial arrest.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
